# ─── Server-only ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set these in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables, for
# Production and Preview. Nothing here reaches the browser: only variables
# prefixed VITE_ are inlined into the JS bundle, and these are read inside the
# serverless functions in api/, never in src/.
#
# The old Next.js repo named these NEXT_PUBLIC_*, which DID ship them to the
# browser. Both spellings work here and the unprefixed name wins, so the values
# already in Vercel keep working. Prefer the unprefixed name for new setups.

# Google Apps Script Web App endpoint. Receives Connect / MSSP / BPL form
# payloads, writes them to the Google Sheet and sends the confirmation email.
# Must be an https:// URL on google.com, or the submission is refused.
# Also accepted: NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL
GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=

# Shown to visitors as the address to write to when a submission cannot be
# recorded, and used by the Apps Script for notifications.
# Also accepted: NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_EMAIL
ADMIN_EMAIL=ask@trenchsecurity.ai

# Optional. Extra origins allowed to post to /api/*, comma-separated. The
# production domains and every Vercel deployment URL are already allowed.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://staging.trenchsecurity.ai

# Optional but recommended. The Apps Script /exec URL is world-postable, so
# anyone who learns it can write sheet rows and trigger emails directly,
# bypassing the rate limit and validation in api/. Set the SAME value as a
# Script Property named SHARED_SECRET in Apps Script
# (Project Settings -> Script Properties) and the script will reject anything
# without it. Configure the Apps Script side FIRST: unset on either side keeps
# the current accept-everything behaviour, so the forms never go offline
# mid-rollout.
# APPS_SCRIPT_SECRET=

# Read by no code, here or in the old repo — the Apps Script holds its own
# reference to the spreadsheet. Setting them in Vercel is harmless but has no
# effect: NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SHEET_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID

# ─── Client-exposed ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only VITE_* reaches the browser. Never put a secret behind this prefix.
# Nothing is required today: forms post to relative /api/* paths.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://www.trenchsecurity.ai
